          "certainty": "possible",
          "reasons": [
           {
            "@type": "meaningComprehension",
            "comprehends": [
             "copies/kj344bw3083#inscription"
            ],
            "note": "Graded low on the figures of the date: the figures could give another date. Pencil, five figures run together at the treble edge, steeply slanted: [8?] 1 1 2 2, i.e. 8.11.22. The month and year are plain; the first figure is two strokes converging on a single bottom bowl with the upper loop left open, the form reading.md warns is an 8 taken for a 6, so the day is either 8 or 6 and I have left date_iso at the month. e2 carries the roll number 1307 in a neater hand, which agrees with the leader label in e4 (WELTE-MIGNON No. 1307, An den Fruehling, Op. 43 No. 1, E. Grieg); e3 shows only ink offsets around the perforations."
           }
          ]
         }
        }
       },
       "medium": "pencil"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
